Serve eCaptureQ on a private Unix socket.

A loopback WebSocket lets any local user subscribe to decrypted plaintext and
leaves a window in which another process can bind the announced port first.
--ecaptureq unix:///DIR/SOCK binds only inside a directory owned by the
current user with no group or other access, sets the socket to 0600 and never
replaces an existing path.

